// A recipe, written from md-docs/recipes/call-wf-from-a-script.md by scripts/docsite/recipes.py;
// edit the recipe, not this file.
page RecipeCallWfFromAScript(path: "/recipes/call-wf-from-a-script", title: "Call WF from a script — Recipes", description: "Call the WebFluent runtime, window.WF, from a script of your own: show a toast, navigate, or read a store, and keep the call in the build.") {
    RecipeShell("Call WF from a script", summary: "The runtime is `window.WF`. A script under `src/`, the console, or a library's callback can call it. This page has a button that copies the page's address, and the script it calls says so with the runtime's toast:", outputs: ["website", "app", "desktop"], since: "", recipes: RECIPE_INDEX, sections: [Anchor(id: "how-it-works", label: "How it works"), Anchor(id: "troubleshooting", label: "Troubleshooting")], related: [RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Call your own JavaScript", to: "/recipes/call-your-own-script"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Hand an element to a script", to: "/recipes/hand-an-element-to-a-script"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Run a script after each page draws", to: "/recipes/listen-for-wf-render")], source: "md-docs/recipes/call-wf-from-a-script.md", how: true, hasVariations: false) {
        code {
            Markdown("**Needs:** the script `src/share.js`, shown below.")
            CodeBlock(#"page Article(path: "/article", title: "Slow roasting", description: "Why we take eleven minutes over it.") {
    Heading("Slow roasting").h1
    Text("Eleven minutes, and why it matters.")
    Button("Copy the link") { on click { shareLink() } }
}"#, title: "wf")
            Markdown("The script is a plain file under `src/` ([Call your own JavaScript](/recipes/call-your-own-script)):")
            CodeBlock(#"// src/share.js
/**
 * Copy this page's address, and say so in a toast.
 */
async function shareLink() {
  try {
    await navigator.clipboard.writeText(location.href);
    WF.toast("Link copied", "success");
  } catch (e) {
    WF.toast("Could not copy the link", "danger");
  }
}"#, title: "js")
        }
        Markdown("- `WF` is on `window` once `app.js` has run, so any script may call it while the page is open. `WF.toast(message, tone, ms)` shows a toast in a tone (`\"info\"` by default) for `ms` milliseconds (3000 by default).\n- Other calls a script makes the same way: `WF.navigate(\"/about\")` moves to another route, and `WF.storeSnapshot(\"Cart\")` reads what a store holds. The [runtime reference](/reference/runtime) lists every function.\n- A build keeps only the runtime modules its code reaches, and it reads your scripts under `src/` for that too: the `WF.toast` written in `src/share.js` keeps the toast module in the build, though no `.wf` code uses it.")

        Callout("A call the build cannot read is not counted: a script in `public/` or from another origin, a `WF[name]` built at run time, or the console. If it reaches a module nothing else uses, set `\"build\": \{ \"runtime\": \"full\" \}`, or the call fails in the browser.", kind: .warning)

        Markdown("A script from another origin must be listed in `meta.scripts`, which widens the policy for it. The build's CSP check refuses an inline `<script>` ([Security](/about/security#ship-a-content-security-policy)).")

        Heading("Troubleshooting", id: "troubleshooting").h2

        Table(caption: "Troubleshooting") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("What you see").header
                    Table.Cell("What to do").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`WF.toast is not a function` (or another runtime function)") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("The build left the module out: write the call in a script under `src/`, or set `\"build\": \{ \"runtime\": \"full\" \}`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`WF is not defined`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("The script ran before `app.js`: call `WF` from an event, a callback or a `wf:render` listener, not at the script's top level") }
                }
            }
        }

    }
}
